agent	Execute Claude Code CLI	2026-10-22T02:33:50.3793352Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdtNGChXTKRojTSe4n3zYd","type":"tool_result","content":"[black-issue-triage v1.0.0] label validation: OK\n{\n  \"marker\": \"[black-issue-triage v1.0.0]\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"final_labels\": [],\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    \"no new labels; if no action is needed call noop instead of add_labels\"\n  ]\n}\n96:_Black_ prefers parentheses over backslashes, and will remove backslashes if found.\n168:parenthesized expressions. Since such expressions are always reformatted to fit minimal\n337:### Parentheses\n339:Some parentheses are optional in the Python grammar. Any expression can be wrapped in a\n340:pair of parentheses to form an atom. There are a few interesting cases:\n353:In those cases, parentheses are removed when the entire statement fits in one line, or\n356:parentheses can also be successfully omitted since the existing bracket pair will\n357:organize the expression neatly anyway. Otherwise, the parentheses are added.\n359:Please note that _Black_ does not add or remove any additional nested parentheses that\n361:parentheses are not going to be removed:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ad8316e-cdf1-4235-8127-0a1fa59b0d21","uuid":"6150adff-9081-4417-9a8d-e1c783c6d439","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:33:50.375Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"[black-issue-triage v1.0.0] label validation: OK\n{\n  \"marker\": \"[black-issue-triage v1.0.0]\",\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"final_labels\": [],\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    \"no new labels; if no action is needed call noop instead of add_labels\"\n  ]\n}\n96:_Black_ prefers parentheses over backslashes, and will remove backslashes if found.\n168:parenthesized expressions. Since such expressions are always reformatted to fit minimal\n337:### Parentheses\n339:Some parentheses are optional in the Python grammar. Any expression can be wrapped in